  "appliesTo": "Licensed pesticide applicators and public operators as defined in G.S. 143-460 using ground equipment; restricted-use applications. Records within 72 hours, kept 3 years. Growers applying on their own or employer's land are excluded.",
  "verification": "researched",
  "notes": "Amount may be formulation or active ingredient per unit of measure. Each day of application is a separate record. Weather is not required by this rule. 2026-09-24 primary-text audit: Who-clause: 02 NCAC 09L .1402 applies to “pesticide applicators, as defined in G.S. 143-460”, which “does not include: a. Any person who uses or supervises the use of a pesticide (i) only for the purpose of producing an agricultural commodity on property owned or rented by him or his employer”. The aerial rule .1002(c) binds all agricultural aircraft operations separately.",
